"Passing the Brass Lantern" by Bernd Eickhoff

player "They say Medea is a sorceress.\nThey say she wields power to deceive.\nThey are wrong.\nSocrates was her father, who created her likeness.\nUlysses her mother, her will to wander and an inquisitive mind.\nShe speakes no truth, but the questions that shake the earth.\nThis story is the undoing of Talos."


verb talk
    takes creature noun
    "There is no one here who will answer."

kind burning: dark, lit

object Brass Lantern, lamp "The lantern is {self burning}"
    instead of examine:
        if self is lit:
            say "The lantern burns with a steady flame."
        else:
            say "The lantern is dark."

man Talos "Bronze sentinel,\nforged protector of his land,\npaces the extend of his limited horizon."

    on give with Brass Lantern:
        say "Not being."
        say "Not reflection."
        say "No wisdom."


room The Isle of Crete "The bronze coast. \nA place of ruin.\nA place of desolation.\nHusks of broken ships litter the horizon. \nNothing moves than the distant hulk of a giant, mindlessly hurling rocks at birds and ships out at sea."

    scenery sea "Water laps listlessly at the shore. A grey sky weighs heavy above."

    scenery bronze coast "The grooves of the giant's steps wearying the stone in endless circumference, since before time."

    scenery ruin, desolation, husks, ships "Flat. Desolate. A world broken in lifeless routine."
    scenery Eris "Gods come and go as they please. Eris seldom lingers."

    on turn 1:
        say "They say Eris drops apples like an orchard in fall."
        say "But that day she appeared in a flash of carbon dioxide"
        say "and dropped a brass lantern at Medea's feet."
        move Brass Lantern to location.

    on turn 2:
        say "Uh oh, the giant is coming this way."

    on turn 3:
        say "You feel the tremor of the earth with his every step."

    on turn 4:
        say "WHOO ARE YOUU? Talos voice booms, reverberating through the emptiness." 
        say "With a grinding of gears the giant comes to a halt."
        move Talos to location.

    on turn 5-:
        say "Talos glowers down on you."


    on give with Brass Lantern:
        if the second is Talos:
            say "Not being."
            say "Not reflection."
            say "No Wisdom."
            say "No Light."

test "default"
    x me. "sorceress"
    take lamp. "taken"
    x lamp. "dark"
    x coast. "grooves"
    x ruin. "Desolate"
    give lamp to talos. "not being"

    
